/users/totoriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T21:57:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T21:57:10Z","body":"I think this is done.\r\n\r\nHere is a test project that I tested all of the things:\r\n\r\n[pull-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24895418/pull-test.zip)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807734364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3983375555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115397#issuecomment-3983375555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115397","id":3983375555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tbXzD","user":{"login":"totoriel","id":132148700,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-Bt3A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132148700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel","html_url":"https://github.com/totoriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/totoriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T10:05:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T10:05:12Z","body":"I think I have made a really big mistake in the development of the new Camera2D changes, because after doing some more testing specifically trying to make a real time strategy game with the new changes I realized that by changing the bounds from bounding the camera view to bounding the camera position, I have made implementing a limited camera bounds a bit troublesome.\n\nAnd to be honest, I don't know what I was thinking when making that change, because it does not make sense to change an already working system for the camera view.\n\nThe problem is that sometimes you can see beyond the position limit, and while that does make sense, it does not make sense to force developers to move their bounds by a few hundred pixels because of a logic change.\nI will revisit this today or tomorrow to see what I can do about it.\n\nI'm thinking to either just add the bounds back, or make the position limit also function as a view bound.\n\nP.S. I feel bad about the fact that I didn't come clean about this from the start, but I did use AI for the documentation. Because English is not my first language, my words may sound out of place or my punctuation may be off, so I used AI to correct my sentences.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3983375555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https:/